74 (~47.7k) -> 1293 (~47.9k) fits entirely inside a ~1000-unit span, with each successive hop following the prior one by roughly 100-500 units, all below the 600-unit latency bound. Volume-based explanations are ruled out: 303 fires once and 1293 three times in the 9600-unit window, the graph is near-tree-like (repeat ratio 0.011), and 303's 4-hop closure contains only 14 nodes, so the path is not one of many coincidental routes.\"\n}\n```", "total_input_tokens": 31680, "total_output_tokens": 7671, "total_tokens": 39351, "total_latency_ms": 95052, "llm_calls": 6, "schema_repairs": 0, "status": "success", "error": ""}